--- !u!114 &818513539
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 818513537}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "In the heart of the Shimmering Labyrinth, a vast crystal city woven from
    glowing runes, every stone pulse declared the magic of merging. Each dawn, light
    poured through fractal windows, painting walking paths in ribbons of color. Here,
    elemental orbs of raw energy drifted along hidden channels\u2014waiting for the
    moment when two identical forms would touch and ignite a new wonder.\nTalia,
    a novice rune-keeper, spent her mornings cataloging stray crystals scattered
    across the labyrinth floors and her evenings tracing faint glyphs etched into
    marble walls. Though curious by nature, she hesitated to bring any two identical
    orbs together\u2014uncertain whether she could bear the responsibility if their
    union failed. \u201CWhat if they shatter?\u201D she whispered, stashing each
    orb in a padded satchel.\nOne afternoon, as a gentle current of prismatic mist
    curled through the corridor, Talia spotted two tiny silver-edged spheres lying
    side by side on a mosaic dais. Their surfaces flickered in perfect sync\u2014an
    unspoken invitation. Heart pounding, she set them together. At first, nothing
    stirred but the soft hum of distant glyphs. Then, a thread of pale light wove
    itself around the pair, drawing them into a single, larger orb that glowed with
    all the colors of sunrise.\nA hush fell across the Labyrinth. Even the whispered
    runes seemed to pause. The new orb hovered, then drifted upward on a column of
    gentle mist, shedding motes of iridescent dust that settled on every nearby rune.
    Each mote carried a fragment of possibility\u2014stories of past mergers and
    future dreams. In that instant, Talia understood that merging was more than a
    mechanical act: it was an opening of hidden potential, a conjuring of new magic
    from simple beginnings.\nFrom that day on, she was called Sparkbearer, the one
    whose first fusion rekindled the Labyrinth\u2019s silent heart. And as she walked
    home beneath glimmering arches, Talia realized she had done far more than merge
    two orbs\u2014she had set the stage for countless stories yet to be born.\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6c42bd4333ae20e45ad610c745f9429a, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -3440902776700696691, guid: 6c42bd4333ae20e45ad610c745f9429a, type: 2}
