--- !u!114 &1889967315
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1889967313}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7fe4e4d5e6f7d4c4a90309ddff04610b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _view: {fileID: 2073268566}
  _screenType: 4
  isActive: 0
  storyImage: {fileID: 210358982}
  title: {fileID: 276468571}
  description: {fileID: 818513539}
  close: {fileID: 1276699867}
  _stories:
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9b9da2aea6fd42148a64a1399f72bd65, type: 3}
    title: The Spark of Fusion
    description: "In the heart of the Shimmering Labyrinth, a vast crystal city woven
      from glowing runes, every stone pulse declared the magic of merging. Each dawn,
      light poured through fractal windows, painting walking paths in ribbons of
      color. Here, elemental orbs of raw energy drifted along hidden channels\u2014waiting
      for the moment when two identical forms would touch and ignite a new wonder.\r\nTalia,
      a novice rune-keeper, spent her mornings cataloging stray crystals scattered
      across the labyrinth floors and her evenings tracing faint glyphs etched into
      marble walls. Though curious by nature, she hesitated to bring any two identical
      orbs together\u2014uncertain whether she could bear the responsibility if their
      union failed. \u201CWhat if they shatter?\u201D she whispered, stashing each
      orb in a padded satchel.\r\nOne afternoon, as a gentle current of prismatic
      mist curled through the corridor, Talia spotted two tiny silver-edged spheres
      lying side by side on a mosaic dais. Their surfaces flickered in perfect sync\u2014an
      unspoken invitation. Heart pounding, she set them together. At first, nothing
      stirred but the soft hum of distant glyphs. Then, a thread of pale light wove
      itself around the pair, drawing them into a single, larger orb that glowed
      with all the colors of sunrise.\r\nA hush fell across the Labyrinth. Even the
      whispered runes seemed to pause. The new orb hovered, then drifted upward on
      a column of gentle mist, shedding motes of iridescent dust that settled on
      every nearby rune. Each mote carried a fragment of possibility\u2014stories
      of past mergers and future dreams. In that instant, Talia understood that merging
      was more than a mechanical act: it was an opening of hidden potential, a conjuring
      of new magic from simple beginnings.\r\nFrom that day on, she was called Sparkbearer,
      the one whose first fusion rekindled the Labyrinth\u2019s silent heart. And
      as she walked home beneath glimmering arches, Talia realized she had done far
      more than merge two orbs\u2014she had set the stage for countless stories yet
      to be born."
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 67e8ff9986c13414999622cf05a68b42, type: 3}
    title: The Convergence Grove
    description: "Beyond the shimmering gates of the Crystal City lay the Convergence
      Grove, where bioluminescent vines draped over stepping-stone paths and glowing
      fruit pulsed like lanterns in still air. Legend held that if two matching fruits
      were pressed together on the ancient Stone Altar, they would fuse into a new
      hybrid\u2014one that carried the essence of both parents and revealed hidden
      grove magic.\r\nMaris, the grove\u2019s quiet caretaker, discovered this truth
      one dewy morning at first light. She had come to gather moon-lily petals for
      the evening rites but paused when she noticed two identical amethyst-hued fruits.
      Their soft glow synchronized in a gentle heartbeat. With reverent care, she
      lifted both and placed them on the carved altar.\r\nA ripple of golden light
      arced between them, and they melted into a single, larger fruit streaked with
      veins of emerald and rose. It hovered for a breath, then drifted skyward, releasing
      a shower of crystalline pollen that floated down to carpet the grove in sparkling
      motes. As each flake settled on her hair and robes, Maris felt a warmth bloom
      in her chest\u2014an acknowledgment that her act of unity had awakened the
      grove\u2019s deepest magic.\r\nFrom that sunrise onward, she tended the Convergence
      Grove with renewed awe. Each day, she selected pairs of like fruits, guiding
      them through their fusions and marveling as novel blossoms unfurled around
      her. Travelers came to witness the spectacle, leaving with vials of pollen
      and fragments of hybrid fruit\u2014gifts of the grove\u2019s rekindled wonder.\r\nThrough
      countless merges, Maris learned that true unity does not erase difference but
      weaves separate strengths into a richer whole. And as the grove thrived in
      ever-changing hues, it stood as living proof: when like meets like with intention
      and care, the world blossoms in unexpected beauty.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c50c4bd0b545a544eb465ba3e4c9d4da, type: 3}
    title: The Mosaic of Echoing Runes
    description: "Within the Grand Hall of PinkoSaga, a vast floor mosaic sprawled
      like a living tapestry, each tile inscribed with ancient runes glowing in cool
      blues, vibrant golds, and sunset crimsons. The hall\u2019s keepers called it
      the Mosaic of Echoing Runes: when two adjacent tiles of the same hue were pressed
      together, their runes would sing a harmony that echoed through the chambers.\r\nJaro,
      a young archivist, spent days studying the mosaic\u2019s inscriptions but never
      dared to merge the tiles\u2014fearing he might silence centuries of lore. One
      evening, curiosity overcame caution. He pressed two sapphire-tinted tiles side
      by side. A low rumble pulsed through the marble, then blossomed into gentle
      chimes dancing across the floor. Encouraged, he traced lines of matching tiles,
      each fusion weaving new melodies and shifting the mosaic\u2019s pattern into
      swirling spirals of silver and ribbons of rose.\r\nWith every merge, the hall
      responded: walls glowed with soft light, sconces brightened in time with the
      melody, and runes across the ceiling shimmered as though awakened from slumber.
      Visitors paused in silent wonder, scholars scribbled fresh notes, and dancers
      moved along the newly formed pathways, guiding their steps to the mosaic\u2019s
      song.\r\nBy night\u2019s end, the Mosaic of Echoing Runes had transformed into
      a kaleidoscope of color and sound. In its center, Jaro performed a final merge
      of two tiles etched with half-forgotten constellations. Their union unlocked
      a hidden trapdoor beneath the floor, revealing a spiral staircase of quartz
      steps descending into the Archives Below. There, he found vaults filled with
      crystalline tomes\u2014repositories of songs, poems, and stories once thought
      lost.\r\nJaro\u2019s first bold merges had done more than animate the mosaic:
      they had opened the gateway to PinkoSaga\u2019s deepest memories. And as he
      lit his lantern and stepped downward, he understood that each careful fusion
      was a key unlocking new worlds of wonder.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: efcc535857891d24885b015b4364b040, type: 3}
    title: The River of Shattered Reflections
    description: "Winding through the heart of PinkoSaga\u2019s citadel was the River
      of Shattered Reflections, its waters like liquid glass reflecting kaleidoscopic
      lights. Within its currents swam small shard-like creatures called glintfish,
      each bearing unique facets of color and song. According to legend, guiding
      two identical glintfish into a shallow alcove would cause them to coalesce
      into a grander artifact\u2014a living token of the river\u2019s magic.\r\nElin,
      apprentice to the river\u2019s guardian, arrived at dawn\u2019s hush with nets
      woven from moon-thread and baskets of star-lily petals\u2014preferred delicacies
      for the glintfish. Patiently, she lured two pale sapphire fish into an alcove
      carved from rose-quartz. When their mirrored scales touched, a soft pulse reverberated
      through the water, and they spiraled into one luminous fish, its facets refracting
      every shade of twilight.\r\nThe hybrid leapt free, leaving behind a single
      golden scale that hovered above the surface. Elin retrieved it, feeling its
      warmth pulse like a heartbeat\u2014an echo of the river\u2019s own flow. Each
      morning thereafter, she repeated the ritual with new pairs: amethyst, emerald,
      topaz\u2014each merge leaving a token scaled in a shrine at the river\u2019s
      source.\r\nOver time, her collection became a gallery of living art: the Shrine
      of Reflections, where tokens shimmered on crystal pedestals and glowed in synchrony
      with the river\u2019s currents. Pilgrims traveled from distant realms to witness
      the merging rituals and leave offerings of dew-sprinkled petals.\r\nOne twilight,
      Elin guided two rare obsidian glintfish into the alcove. Their fusion birthed
      a colossal fish whose scales held every hue of night\u2019s sky. It swirled
      in the water then burst into a cascade of spectral ribbons that arced over
      the city gates\u2014heralding a new era of unity between river and realm. And
      in that luminous moment, the people of PinkoSaga realized that the true magic
      of merging lay not in the tokens themselves, but in the patient care and wonder
      that shaped them.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5719fd0b428c171439ec736824cac4b6, type: 3}
    title: The Tapestry of Living Light
    description: "Above the Citadel\u2019s Lantern Court, weavers threaded strands
      of captured starlight into vast tapestry frames. Each fiber glowed with pulsing
      brilliance, and whenever two identical strands were intertwined, new patterns
      rippled across the fabric\u2014night skies filled with constellations and dawn
      fields awash in aurora.\r\nRina, an aspiring master weaver, hesitated before
      her loom\u2014afraid her first intentional merge might unravel the court\u2019s
      careful balance. But one starlit eve, she found two leftover threads of moonlight
      silver, their soft glow beckoning. With trembling fingers, she guided them
      into the warp, whispering prayers to the light. The tapestry pulsed in response,
      and a new pattern bloomed: twin arcs of heavenly wings spreading across the
      cloth in golden radiance.\r\nFrom the frame, a sliver of living light detached
      and drifted upward, merging with the sky itself. Above, the actual stars shimmered
      in unison, as though echoing her creation. The Lantern Court gasped in awe
      as Rina\u2019s single merge transformed both tapestry and heavens.\r\nEncouraged,
      she continued weaving: dusk-rose threads and sapphirine blue, each pairing
      birthing new celestial motifs. Pilgrims gathered beneath the tapestry to witness
      her merges, and soon the court\u2019s nightly ceremonies became celebrations
      of runic light and cosmic harmony.\r\nThrough her work, Rina discovered that
      weaving and merging were one craft: each intentional union of strands conjured
      new patterns in the world above. And as the tapestry of living light grew to
      span the court wall, it stood as a testament to the creative power tucked within
      every brave merge.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 09660cc31d3ceb04aa50eec6aa1eb131, type: 3}
    title: The Mirror Pool
    description: "Hidden in the Crystal Gardens lay a circular pool whose surface
      was as smooth as glossed obsidian. They called it the Mirror Pool\u2014where
      two matching offerings dropped together would cause the water to swirl and
      reveal visions in its depths.\r\nOrin, a novice dream-reader, carried two glass
      talismans etched with rune-circles\u2014gifts from the Shrine of Reflections.
      At dawn\u2019s quiet, he released them side by side into the pool. Ripples
      spun outward, then coalesced into a spiral of liquid starlight. Within the
      vortex appeared an image of a stone chamber lined with scroll-filled alcoves.
      The vision shimmered, then vanished, leaving Orin breathless: he had glimpsed
      PinkoSaga\u2019s long-lost Archives Below.\r\nEach day thereafter, he returned
      with paired offerings\u2014silver-leaf bowls, crystal petals, carved rune-stones.
      Every merge unlocked a new fragment: hidden hallways, whispered histories,
      murals that told of ancient councils. He documented each glimpse in a bound
      journal, sketching corridors and slaves of forgotten lore.\r\nFinally, with
      two golden prism-shards, he performed his boldest merge. The pool erupted in
      slow-motion roars of light. The garden\u2019s mosaic floor creaked and slid
      apart, revealing steps descending into starlit darkness. Lantern in hand, Orin
      stepped down\u2014into a repository of living memory, where scrolls floated
      in luminous filigree. The Mirror Pool had done more than show visions: it had
      forged a path into the heart of PinkoSaga\u2019s secret past.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: db294753acc16ec42b64521dd8384945, type: 3}
    title: The Skybound Aviary
    description: "Suspended between towering spire-pillars of crystalline glass,
      the Skybound Aviary was home to winged marvels\u2014feather-sprites, glimmer-jellies,
      and scale-wing hybrids that danced on gentle updrafts. Whenever two identical
      creatures soared together along converging airstreams, they merged into a singular
      wonder of enhanced beauty and strength.\r\nTess, an apprentice aviary-keeper,
      tended to the pens of pastel-feathered sprites, coaxing them with dew-sprinkled
      berries and soft song. Though gentle by nature, she hesitated at the fuse-platform\u2014afraid
      she might misalign their currents and break their delicate forms. One gold-hued
      dawn, she guided two cerulean glimmer-jellies into a merging current. The air
      shimmered as their bodies flickered in unison, then coalesced into a larger
      jelly whose wings refracted sunrise hues.\r\nThe hybrid arcs soared overhead,
      tracing patterns of rainbow mist across the Aviary\u2019s skywalks. Tess watched,
      tears of joy in her eyes, as the creature danced on currents she had helped
      shape. Encouraged, she tended more merges: scale-wing pups and gleam-feather
      fawns\u2014each fusion birthing creatures that blended speed, song, and soft
      glow.\r\nVisitors rode tethered sky-platforms to glimpse these marvels. Minstrels
      composed ballads in their honor, and aviary-artists sketched every loop and
      flutter. Through Tess\u2019s merges, the Aviary became a living testament to
      cooperation and wonder\u2014proof that guiding two souls together can shape
      not only the sky but the hearts of all who watch.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bd88aaf2f256c0e409a10eb53510d2f1, type: 3}
    title: The Forgotten Conduit
    description: "In the deep vaults beneath the Arcane Foundry lay the Forgotten
      Conduit, a circular chamber ringed with dormant rune-pillars and sealed portals.
      At its center stood pedestals holding paired arc-crystals\u2014long unused
      fragments of raw magic. Legend said that placing two matching crystals side
      by side would awaken the Conduit\u2019s power, forging gateways to distant
      realms of PinkoSaga.\r\nKyran, a wandering mage-scholar, braved the Foundry\u2019s
      labyrinthine corridors at dusk. He carried two identically inscribed rune-crystals\u2014treasures
      from a desert ruin. With steady hands, he set them on the pedestals. The pillars
      trembled, veins of faint glow spidered along the walls, and a ring of wavering
      light formed overhead, projecting glimpses of floating libraries, glowing groves,
      and hidden caverns.\r\nNight after night, Kyran returned with new pairs\u2014moonstone,
      tide-ring, mirror-shard\u2014each merge reopening the portal to reveal fresh
      vistas. He charted these realms in a leather grimoire, drawing maps by the
      portal\u2019s pale glow. Fellow explorers followed, offering their own crystal
      pairs in hopes of discovery.\r\nFinally, with two golden dawn-crystals, Kyran
      performed his boldest merge. The Conduit roared in living light, and a stable
      gateway opened beyond the pedestals\u2014a corridor of shifting runes leading
      to a realm where magic itself shaped the sky. Stepping through, Kyran vanished
      into legend, while the Forgotten Conduit stood reborn\u2014its ancient power
      renewed by the courage of a seeker who dared to merge the known with the unknown.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: db96a1765841d7640b0114623583d862, type: 3}
    title: The Crystal Atrium
    description: "Beneath a vaulted dome of chromatic glass stood the Crystal Atrium,
      where luminous buds bloomed like faceted flowers. Each bud absorbed ambient
      light and refracted it into prismatic displays. When two matching buds were
      pressed together on the central dais, they fused into a towering bloom that
      bathed the Atrium in colors unseen.\r\nSeren, caretaker of the Atrium, rose
      each dawn to prune delicate facets and nourish their roots with dew-distilled
      starlight. Yet she had never dared to merge the blooms\u2014fearing missteps
      might shatter them. One pale morning, she found two lavender-hued buds pulsing
      side by side. Gathering resolve, she brought them to the dais.\r\nA filament
      of silver light threaded between the petals, drawing them into a spiraling
      embrace. In a flash of refracted brilliance, the new bloom towered above her,
      its facets shifting through violet, rose, amber, and gold. Sunbeams through
      the dome bent to its glow, scattering rainbows across every column and leaf.\r\nPilgrims
      arrived at the Atrium\u2019s archways, offering dew-vials and crystal shards
      to try their own merges. Under Seren\u2019s guidance, they formed circles on
      the dais, each merge adding new hues to the collective spectacle. The Atrium
      became a living symphony of light, each fusion a note in an ever-evolving concerto.\r\nThrough
      her work, Seren learned that creation required trust and intention. Each bloom
      was a testament to the harmony possible when two like forms unite. And as the
      Crystal Atrium\u2019s colors flourished beneath the dome, she knew her single
      act of courage had illuminated not just the garden, but every heart drawn to
      its gentle glow.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 09f15d739f700a44b9829b2a1595df34, type: 3}
    title: The Luminous Passage
    description: "Deep beneath the city\u2019s catacombs ran the Luminous Passage,
      a tunnel carved from pearl-white stone and veined with glowing runes. Lanterns
      of captured stardust flickered at intervals, guiding weary pilgrims through
      its silent depths. At the tunnel\u2019s midpoint stood two pedestals bearing
      identical quartz orbs\u2014etched with swirling glyphs. Tradition held that
      placing both orbs together would trigger a cascade of living light, illuminating
      the way forward.\r\nAren, a traveler seeking refuge from his restless thoughts,
      entered at twilight. His lantern dimmed as he walked, shadows dancing on the
      walls. Reaching the central dais, he set one orb on the left pedestal, then
      paused\u2014uncertain of his worthiness. Gathering courage, he placed the second
      orb beside it.\r\nThe pedestals quivered; veins of light flared in the stone.
      Soft luminescence pooled around Aren\u2019s feet, spiraling upward to form
      an arch of living light. The runes on the walls glowed in concentric waves,
      their inscriptions revealing messages of hope, courage, and unity for all who
      walked the path.\r\nAs the passage brightened, Aren felt his burdens lift.
      Each step toward the exit felt lighter, guided by the gentle glow of the merged
      orbs. Following in his footsteps, others placed their own quartz orbs on the
      dais, extending the ribbon of light deeper into the catacombs.\r\nWhen Aren
      emerged at the far end\u2014into a courtyard bathed in dawn\u2019s first blush\u2014he
      carried with him a single quartz shard pulsing with the Passage\u2019s glow.
      He realized merging had guided him not only through stone tunnels but through
      his own shadows. And as he gazed back at the arch of light behind him, he understood:
      the Luminous Passage was more than a corridor\u2014it was a living testament
      to unity\u2019s power, lighting the way for all who sought their path.\r"
